      "writtenOn": "2026-11-19T11:29:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, keeping the bitmap then.\n\nOn the REKEY_SA case: confirmed by reading this patch set. The dispatcher calls ikev2_sa_free_all_child_sa() on sa-\u003echilds and keeps only childs[0]\u0027s IDs as the old IDs, so a sibling Child in slot 1 is neither kept nor scanned, and the allocator can pick its still-installed ID. Later changes of this chain (the rekey fixes behind it) replace only the named Child, which is why it does not show there, but this change must not depend on them.\n\nI will fix it here: on a rekey, replace only the rekeyed Child and keep the others, so the scan sees every installed ID, and add the regression you describe (rekey while a sibling Child stays live, IDs distinct, SAD entries and the replacement SPI present). I will send a new patch set once it is verified.",
